[2] Flower from turning 1/pi radians
  theta=1/pi = 0.318309886183790671537767526745 radians
  radian-residue quotient:
    1/pi ~= 7/22, so the model step on Z/22 is +7.
    gcd(7,22)=1, hence all 22 radian-residue families are visited.
    after 22 petals, actual angle differs from 7 radians by 0.002817496043394773830886.
    max deviation from the 7/22 family grid over the first 22 petals is 0.002689428041422284111300.
  full-circle quotient guardrail:
    rotation number is theta/(2*pi)=1/(2*pi^2)=0.050660591821168885721939731605.
    best   le_22: 1/20 err=0.000660591821168885721940
    best  le_100: 4/79 err=0.000027680428763822430800
    best  le_300: 15/296 err=0.000015083854506789953736
    best le_1000: 23/454 err=2.01130372964498325E-7
    substituting 22/7 gives full-circle model 49/968.
  readout:
    the 22 families are a real radian-address quotient, not a true
    circle-closing period.  This is analogous to C27 shell transfer:
    a useful quotient is allowed only after its forgotten geometry is named.

[3] Geometric and algebraic unital distinctions
  q=2: 2-(9,3,1) blocks=12 rep=4
  q=3: 2-(28,4,1) blocks=63 rep=9  <-- v=28=2*14, v-1=27=C, k=4, b=63=7*9
  q=4: 2-(65,5,1) blocks=208 rep=16
  q=3 package:
    q^3+1=28 equals the 2*14 antipodal/apex point count.
    q^3=27 equals the C=2*14-1 shell in HYP-2937.
    q+1=4 is the block size, and q^3+(q+1)=31.
    Thus cuberoot(31) is a cubic-shell mnemonic: 31=27+4.
  algebraic unital guardrail:
    geometric unitals, unit groups, and unital maps are different.
    For LRC14, the useful algebraic rule is unit preservation:
    quotient maps should send the identity/floor object to the
    identity carrier rather than erasing AP/GW or unit-visible shells.

